---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import SectionHead from '~/components/SectionHead.astro'
import Logo from '~/components/Logo.astro'
import { SITE } from '~/data/site'

const adoption = [
  {
    step: '01',
    name: 'Bring your corpus',
    body: 'Metanorma-authored documents enter with their full structure — clause anchors, typed units, models. Other sources join as their structure is verified; every chunk records its provenance.',
  },
  {
    step: '02',
    name: 'Declare your profile',
    body: 'The publisher declares its profile: publication identifiers, terminology, model coverage, prompt templates and thresholds. The publisher owns the content, the profile and the frontend.',
  },
  {
    step: '03',
    name: 'Serve under your brand',
    body: 'Konneal builds the databases and serves the API. The deployment is white-labeled to your organization, with a small credit beside your emblem.',
  },
]
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Deployments"
  description="The Konneal engine in production: the OIML SMART AI reference deployment, white-labeled deployments for standards organizations, and the adoption path."
>
  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-14 pt-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-16">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="tick"></span>Deployments</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-serif text-[2.2rem] font-medium leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.01em] sm:text-[2.9rem]">
        One engine, many standards bodies.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[1.04rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Konneal is the publisher-agnostic serving layer: retrieval, the answer contract, verdicts and the measurement
        gates, applied to each organization’s own corpus under its own name.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.2fr)_minmax(0,1fr)]">
        <div>
          <SectionHead
            eyebrow="The reference"
            title={`${SITE.reference.name} — live since the engine’s first promotion`}
            lede="The public question-answering service of the International Organization of Legal Metrology: close to 900 publications, 9.3 million words, 9 languages — cited answers, computed verdicts, and the full measurement discipline, purely on open-weight models."
          />
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
            <a
              href={SITE.reference.url}
              class="border border-blue bg-blue px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.85rem] text-white transition-colors hover:bg-[#1c2f73]"
            >
              ai.oimlsmart.org ↗
            </a>
            <a
              href={SITE.reference.howItWorksUrl}
              class="border border-rule bg-surface px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.85rem] text-blue transition-colors hover:border-keyline"
            >
              How it works, for its readers ↗
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-ink-faint">
            The engine behind it — hybrid retrieval over clause-structured corpora, the answer contract, conformance
            by execution, the evaluation gates — is the same package every deployment consumes. Promotion there is
            gated by the same golden suites that grade the live service.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col justify-center gap-8 border border-rule bg-surface p-8">
          <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-6 font-mono text-[0.78rem]">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-ink-faint">publications</dt>
              <dd class="text-[1.3rem] font-medium text-blue">≈ 900</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-ink-faint">words</dt>
              <dd class="text-[1.3rem] font-medium text-blue">9.3 M</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-ink-faint">languages</dt>
              <dd class="text-[1.3rem] font-medium text-blue">9</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-ink-faint">defined terms</dt>
              <dd class="text-[1.3rem] font-medium text-blue">≈ 9 000</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-ink-faint">bibliographic records</dt>
              <dd class="text-[1.3rem] font-medium text-blue">5 707</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-ink-faint">publication families</dt>
              <dd class="text-[1.3rem] font-medium text-blue">224</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
        <div>
          <SectionHead
            eyebrow="White label"
            title="“[SDO] Answers, powered by Konneal”"
            lede="Each deployment carries the organization’s emblem and name; Konneal appears only in a small credit — the same discipline as the mark itself: present, precise, never loud."
          />
          <p class="mt-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            The credit lockup is specified in the brand: “Powered by” set in the regular weight at reduced ink, the
            mark at 1.4 × the wordmark’s x-height, baseline-aligned. It sits beside institutional emblems, not above
            them.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center border border-rule bg-surface p-12">
          <Logo variant="light" lockup="credit" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
      <SectionHead eyebrow="Adoption" title="Three steps to your deployment" />
      <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-px overflow-hidden border border-rule bg-rule md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          adoption.map((a) => (
            <li class="bg-surface p-7">
              <p class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] text-blue">{a.step}</p>
              <h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-[1.2rem] font-medium">{a.name}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2.5 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">{a.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-sm text-ink-faint">
        The reference adapters run on Cloudflare (Workers, Vectorize, D1, KV, R2); the ports are seams, so any platform
        providing model serving, vector search and durable storage can carry a deployment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
